<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Committee of Safety (Hawaii)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1893</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Committee of Safety was a group of 13 mostly American and European businessmen and lawyers in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honolulu">Honolulu</a> who organised the overthrow of the Hawaiian Kingdom in January 1893. Led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorrin-a-thurston">Lorrin A. Thurston</a>, it acted after Queen Liliʻuokalani tried to issue a new constitution restoring royal power, and with the support of US marines it proclaimed the Provisional Government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanford-b-dole">Sanford B. Dole</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/committee-of-safety-hawaii.jpg" alt="Committee of Safety (Hawaii)" width="320" height="306" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hawaiian_League_(PP-36-3-005).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
